      {
        "id": "p52-q19-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Sketch the curve and state its range.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y<0$ or $y\\ge e$.",
          "worked": "There are no intercepts because $e^x>0$ and $x=0$ is excluded.\n\nAs $x\\to0^-$, $y\\to-\\infty$; as $x\\to0^+$, $y\\to+\\infty$. Thus $x=0$ is a vertical asymptote.\n\nAs $x\\to-\\infty$, $y\\to0^-$, so the negative branch approaches the horizontal asymptote $y=0$ from below. As $x\\to+\\infty$, $y\\to+\\infty$.\n\nUsing the slope and concavity results from part b, draw a decreasing, concave-down negative branch and a concave-up positive branch with minimum $(1,e)$. The negative branch takes every value below zero, and the positive branch takes every value at least $e$.\n\nRange: $(-\\infty,0)\\cup[e,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
